otal":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"<!-- Before creating an issue please make sure you are using the latest version of webpack. -->\r\n\r\n**Do you want to request a *feature* or report a *bug*?**\r\n<!-- Please ask questions on StackOverflow or the webpack Gitter (https://gitter.im/webpack/webpack). Questions will be closed. -->\r\nBug\r\n\r\n**What is the current behavior?**\r\nModules have no exports when they are circularly imported.\r\n\r\nIn the example given below, `b.js` can't access the exported variable `a` of `index.js`.\r\n\r\n**If the current behavior is a bug, please provide the steps to reproduce.**\r\n<!-- A great way to do this is to provide your configuration via a GitHub gist. -->\r\nUse the code from this gist:\r\nhttps://gist.github.com/gustavohenke/835d64b4049b2c71eeba811fceb8c481\r\n\r\nthen:\r\n```\r\nwebpack\r\nnode bundle.js\r\n// will print undefined\r\n```\r\n\r\n**What is the expected behavior?**\r\nThe currently exported variables should be available, even though there's a circular dependency,\r\njust like plain CommonJS does.\r\n\r\nIn the above example, running the bundle file should print `123`.\r\n\r\n**Please mention other relevant information such as the browser version, Node.js version, Operating System and programming language.**\r\nUsing Windows 10 and Node v6.7.0, with plain JavaScript.\r\nNo browser used.","closed_by":{"login":"sokra","id":1365881,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjU4ODE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1365881?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sokra","html_url":"https://github.com/sokra","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sokra/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sokra/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sokra/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sokra/starred{/owner}{/repo